WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:30.110 --> 00:01:34.490
<b>The Legendary Hero</b>

3
00:01:35.190 --> 00:01:38.820
We got some big news!
Captain Koby has escaped!

4
00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:40.160
<b>Beehive, the Pirate Island
New World</b>

5
00:01:38.860 --> 00:01:40.320
Are you serious?!

6
00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:43.570
Aw,
yeah! If he's free,

7
00:01:43.630 --> 00:01:46.060
the Commodore can't stop
us from goin' after him.

8
00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:48.720
We'll be set for life if we
can catch him ourselves!

9
00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:50.400
Then what
the hell are we waitin' for?

10
00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:54.250
Alright! He's already got a bounty,
so we'll be good to go!

11
00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:56.560
All we gotta do is take
his head to Cross Guild!

12
00:01:56.590 --> 00:01:59.470
Hell yeah. I bought odds
on him with a Win ticket

13
00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:01.420
and the payout's
gonna be huge!

14
00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:03.820
How much
will we get if we kill him?

15
00:02:03.820 --> 00:02:06.110
Heh. You might wanna
sit down for this one.

16
00:02:06.110 --> 00:02:08.650
His bounty is five stars!

17
00:02:08.730 --> 00:02:11.030
That means he's worth
five treasure chests...

18
00:02:11.050 --> 00:02:13.520
500 million berries!

19
00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:16.070
Captains are usually
only worth one star!

20
00:02:16.150 --> 00:02:18.560
They must really want
this guy dead, huh?

21
00:02:21.350 --> 00:02:23.760
Alright,
men! The hunt is on!

22
00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:26.150
We're about to hit
the jackpot!

23
00:02:29.260 --> 00:02:32.280
I've got an itch
on the left side of my chest.

24
00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:35.570
That's where the slaves
are held before the sale.

25
00:02:35.720 --> 00:02:37.100
Huh?

26
00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:44.420
Are you kitten
me? They're escaping!

27
00:02:44.420 --> 00:02:46.720
The slaves are runnin' for it?

28
00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:49.930
Yeah! That means we
can hunt 'em down! Oh, boy!

29
00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:51.790
Don't
even think ameowt it!

30
00:02:51.860 --> 00:02:53.550
Keep your claws in check!

31
00:02:53.550 --> 00:02:56.810
Bring 'em back! Now!
And you better not kill Koby!

32
00:02:57.170 --> 00:02:59.670
Or I'll make sure you
answer to Teach!

33
00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:03.870
Uh. Wait, did that
rock just talk?

34
00:03:03.880 --> 00:03:06.300
No. Pizarro
knows that we're here!

35
00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:07.800
We need to run!

36
00:03:12.630 --> 00:03:14.290
We're
not gonna make it.

37
00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:18.090
Please, Koby, you need to get
out of here while you still can.

38
00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:19.710
Don't let us slow you down.

39
00:03:19.790 --> 00:03:21.910
I promised that I'd
help you escape,

40
00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:24.680
and you will, by
using me as bait!

41
00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:25.690
Run as fast as you can!

42
00:03:25.690 --> 00:03:28.930
And no matter what, don't
let the pirates catch you!

43
00:03:28.930 --> 00:03:32.570
Go! I'll see you all again soon!

44
00:03:38.210 --> 00:03:40.490
Thank you, Captain Koby.

45
00:03:43.540 --> 00:03:45.270
You're a living saint!

46
00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:53.550
<b>Shiryu of the Rain
Clear-Clear Fruit
Invisible Man</b>

47
00:03:54.730 --> 00:03:55.990
Why
don't you capture

48
00:03:55.990 --> 00:03:59.280
the damned slaves
yourself, Pizarro?

49
00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:06.790
'Cause I don't want Teach
to come back and chew meowt.

50
00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:08.480
<b>"Corrupt King" Avalo Pizarro
Isle-Isle Fruit
Island Man</b>

51
00:04:09.370 --> 00:04:10.460
Whenever
I move too much,

52
00:04:10.460 --> 00:04:13.920
I end up breaking things
and it's a huge mess. Hm?

53
00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:19.880
Why don't I stop 'em, huh?

54
00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:23.600
Furget it, Vasco.
What are you gonna do?

55
00:04:24.620 --> 00:04:25.660
I'll save you.

56
00:04:29.020 --> 00:04:30.640
If I set the town on fire,

57
00:04:30.640 --> 00:04:33.520
they'll have nowhere
to run, right?

58
00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:35.130
<b>"Heavy Drinker" Vasco Shot
Glug-Glug Fruit
Booze Man</b>

59
00:04:42.590 --> 00:04:45.260
That would be
a complete cat-tastrophe!

60
00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:48.880
Don't you dare! Teach
is gonna be furry-ous!

61
00:04:48.880 --> 00:04:51.360
Eh, what's that?
Burn 'em, you said?

62
00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:54.100
Absolutely no
burning anyone, you hear me?

63
00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:56.760
We just finished
repairing Rocky Port!

64
00:04:56.820 --> 00:05:01.360
Alright, have it your way.
We'll let Wolf handle it.

65
00:05:02.910 --> 00:05:05.910
Wait, Wolf?

66
00:05:05.830 --> 00:05:10.040
<b>"Colossal Battleship" Sanjuan Wolf
Huge-Huge Fruit
Gigantification Man</b>

67
00:05:07.880 --> 00:05:10.260
That's the worst
idea I've ever heard!

68
00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:13.470
He'll crush the whole
town into kitty litter!

69
00:05:17.320 --> 00:05:18.320
Over here!

70
00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:24.840
Damn it, what am I
supposed to do now?

71
00:05:25.150 --> 00:05:26.990
I can't keep running
away forever!

72
00:05:29.210 --> 00:05:31.050
I'll be okay.

73
00:05:31.260 --> 00:05:34.180
I just have to hold out until
the others can get out of here.

74
00:05:34.260 --> 00:05:36.380
I'll figure out
the rest after that!

75
00:05:36.380 --> 00:05:39.530
Well, well.
Koby the Hero!

76
00:05:42.700 --> 00:05:49.420
I'm so glad you're here, Koby.
'Cause I've got big plans.

77
00:05:49.470 --> 00:05:52.470
I'm gonna turn Pirate Island...

78
00:05:55.290 --> 00:05:57.830
...into a full-fledged country!

79
00:05:58.180 --> 00:06:02.530
One that flies the flag
of the World Government!

80
00:06:02.230 --> 00:06:07.980
And that'll make me a king
of the Blackbeard Kingdom!

81
00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:12.240
So what d'you think?

82
00:06:13.300 --> 00:06:15.710
I think your plan's as
ridiculous as you are.

83
00:06:15.790 --> 00:06:18.230
You really think the Government
would agree to that?

84
00:06:18.310 --> 00:06:20.310
To a country made
up of criminals?

85
00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:24.650
Hey! Don't you know it's rude
to stomp on someone's dream?

86
00:06:24.820 --> 00:06:26.190
They might see it my way,

87
00:06:26.190 --> 00:06:29.950
now I've got you as
a bargaining chip.

88
00:06:29.950 --> 00:06:31.690
The day the Navy
negotiates with terrorists

89
00:06:31.690 --> 00:06:34.250
will be the day justice dies!

90
00:06:34.250 --> 00:06:39.010
And I won't be your bargaining
chip. I can't be.

91
00:06:39.010 --> 00:06:41.060
I'm a member of SWORD!

92
00:06:42.060 --> 00:06:45.910
Huh? The hell is SWORD?
Never heard of it.

93
00:06:46.070 --> 00:06:47.700
So that's how it is.

94
00:06:47.890 --> 00:06:48.850
Huh?

95
00:06:48.880 --> 00:06:50.570
This will not end well.

96
00:06:50.600 --> 00:06:53.190
Call off the trade,
Teach. It won't work.

97
00:06:53.190 --> 00:06:54.390
Huh?

98
00:06:54.440 --> 00:06:56.820
Let me explain.

99
00:07:01.850 --> 00:07:02.630
Since this kid's from SWORD,

100
00:07:02.630 --> 00:07:05.410
that means he's a Marine,
but not officially.

101
00:07:07.810 --> 00:07:10.480
SWORD members
surrender their Navy Code.

102
00:07:08.980 --> 00:07:09.810
Huh?

103
00:07:11.260 --> 00:07:13.120
They aren't like
their comrades.

104
00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:16.290
They're Marines who have
submitted their resignations.

105
00:07:17.020 --> 00:07:19.180
They can pick fights
with the Four Emperors

106
00:07:19.790 --> 00:07:22.460
without permission
from above.

107
00:07:22.460 --> 00:07:25.220
They can also disregard
orders at their discretion

108
00:07:25.220 --> 00:07:27.050
and move as they like.

109
00:07:26.510 --> 00:07:27.750
And that's the issue.

110
00:07:28.430 --> 00:07:31.010
The Navy is absolved
of all responsibility

111
00:07:31.640 --> 00:07:33.600
for their actions.

112
00:07:33.610 --> 00:07:36.140
They can cut them
loose as they see fit.

113
00:07:38.060 --> 00:07:39.410
Ain't that cute!

114
00:07:39.770 --> 00:07:41.650
Most Marines just
sit on their asses,

115
00:07:41.820 --> 00:07:44.360
waiting for daddy's
permission to fight us.

116
00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:47.650
But you do what you like,
consequences be damned!

117
00:07:49.880 --> 00:07:53.510
I get it now! I like your style!

118
00:07:53.820 --> 00:07:57.580
That said, I'm not gonna
change my plan!

119
00:07:57.580 --> 00:08:00.050
'Cause you're a special case!

120
00:08:01.090 --> 00:08:04.090
Doesn't matter if you're
with SWORD or not.

121
00:08:04.350 --> 00:08:07.380
The public won't like it if
the Navy abandons you.

122
00:08:07.940 --> 00:08:11.680
It's bad press to turn
your back on a hero, right?

123
00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:14.660
Your life's
in the people's hands.

124
00:08:15.040 --> 00:08:16.420
Looks like the World
Government

125
00:08:16.420 --> 00:08:19.220
will lose credibility either way!

126
00:08:21.570 --> 00:08:25.990
I think he gets the message.
We're done here.

127
00:08:26.210 --> 00:08:30.630
Lock him up and don't
let him escape!

128
00:08:33.290 --> 00:08:34.470
Get
back here, Koby!

129
00:08:41.100 --> 00:08:42.210
Here's the deal.

130
00:08:42.510 --> 00:08:45.220
I'll unlock this door
for you, and in return,

131
00:08:45.220 --> 00:08:49.560
you'll free Master Moria
from his cell, deeper inside.

132
00:08:48.380 --> 00:08:51.620
Guess this is what I
deserve for helping a pirate!

133
00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:53.800
But necessity knows no law!

134
00:09:00.010 --> 00:09:00.810
Huh?

135
00:09:01.970 --> 00:09:02.970
The hell's that?

136
00:09:12.690 --> 00:09:16.030
Three Marines
just showed up at the port!

137
00:09:16.030 --> 00:09:18.750
Huh? Marines? That can't be!

138
00:09:18.750 --> 00:09:19.580
Hurry up!

139
00:09:21.610 --> 00:09:23.950
They're
strong! Be careful!

140
00:09:25.710 --> 00:09:27.520
Did someone
come to rescue me?

141
00:09:27.550 --> 00:09:30.850
No, stop it, Koby, this is
not the time for your selfishness!

142
00:09:30.850 --> 00:09:33.020
What is wrong with me?

143
00:09:52.040 --> 00:09:54.000
Who are
they? They're monsters!

144
00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:54.920
Looks
like they're headed

145
00:09:55.000 --> 00:09:56.470
straight to the center of town!

146
00:09:56.470 --> 00:09:57.920
What do they want from us?

147
00:09:57.920 --> 00:10:00.460
I don't know! Just shoot!

148
00:10:07.770 --> 00:10:10.270
What? They didn't even flinch!

149
00:10:10.590 --> 00:10:13.980
End
of the line, monster!

150
00:10:16.190 --> 00:10:18.980
Whoa!
His head came off!

151
00:10:21.320 --> 00:10:25.370
Woohoo! Y'see
that? That's how it's done!

152
00:10:25.730 --> 00:10:27.270
They're not so tough now!

153
00:10:29.410 --> 00:10:31.070
Huh?

154
00:10:33.170 --> 00:10:34.760
That hurt.

155
00:10:34.840 --> 00:10:37.000
Huh? He's a logia-type!

156
00:10:37.510 --> 00:10:39.470
What the hell
is wrong with him?

157
00:10:39.550 --> 00:10:41.370
His body's like clay!

158
00:10:42.330 --> 00:10:44.690
Where
are you, Koby?!

159
00:10:47.210 --> 00:10:48.450
Hey, look over there!

160
00:10:49.200 --> 00:10:51.870
I swear I just saw those
buildings move on their own!

161
00:10:51.900 --> 00:10:53.610
Yeah, sure they did, pal!

162
00:10:53.650 --> 00:10:55.830
How's quitting
drinking going for ya?

163
00:11:03.740 --> 00:11:05.490
Be good
and do as I say!

164
00:11:08.440 --> 00:11:10.400
Now march forward!

165
00:11:10.420 --> 00:11:13.300
Is she whipping that
building? That's weird.

166
00:11:13.300 --> 00:11:16.100
Come on. Where's
your stamina?

167
00:11:18.280 --> 00:11:22.740
Is that really the best
you can do? You are so pathetic!

168
00:11:23.110 --> 00:11:25.760
I kinda feel like
we shouldn't be watching this.

169
00:11:26.370 --> 00:11:28.600
Hi, boys. Finished staring?

170
00:11:28.600 --> 00:11:32.930
Uh! We, uh...
Wait, that mark!

171
00:11:39.960 --> 00:11:43.200
You pirates act like you've
never seen a Marine before.

172
00:11:43.020 --> 00:11:46.480
<b>Rear Admiral Kujaku
Marine Headquarters (SWORD)
Granddaughter of "Master Tactician" Tsuru
Whip-Whip Fruit
Discipline Woman</b>

173
00:11:46.120 --> 00:11:50.720
How adorable.
Come here.

174
00:11:57.830 --> 00:11:59.980
Let me teach you a lesson.

175
00:12:00.060 --> 00:12:00.890
Ha ha ha ha!

176
00:12:09.130 --> 00:12:11.460
What now?
I'm done for!

177
00:12:16.380 --> 00:12:18.430
Eyes
on the target, boys!

178
00:12:21.990 --> 00:12:23.870
Ready. Aim. Fire!

179
00:12:46.340 --> 00:12:49.510
What? What?

180
00:12:49.510 --> 00:12:51.850
What?

181
00:12:52.810 --> 00:12:55.730
Oh, my! How lovely!

182
00:12:55.730 --> 00:12:58.230
Wait, no! What is this?

183
00:12:58.930 --> 00:13:01.550
Where are these goddamn
flowers coming from?

184
00:13:01.550 --> 00:13:04.940
Wait, I've seen this.

185
00:13:04.940 --> 00:13:05.970
Of course!

186
00:13:09.320 --> 00:13:11.510
Dr.
Vegapunk invented this!

187
00:13:15.660 --> 00:13:19.970
In fact, it earned
him the Mobel Peace Prize!

188
00:13:19.970 --> 00:13:22.400
Nobody cares
about that, okay?!

189
00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:24.800
Who the hell did
this to our guns?

190
00:13:25.140 --> 00:13:25.850
Hey, Koby!

191
00:13:29.640 --> 00:13:31.460
Come here
and stay close to me!

192
00:13:31.460 --> 00:13:34.660
Uh. Uh.
But not in a weird way!

193
00:13:34.590 --> 00:13:38.380
<b>Commander Hibari
Marine Headquarters
(SWORD)</b>

194
00:13:38.500 --> 00:13:43.000
Wait, Hibari? What are you
doing here? Are those...?

195
00:13:43.000 --> 00:13:45.040
That's right. They're
Flower Rounds.

196
00:13:45.040 --> 00:13:47.710
But they won't last;
we have to hurry!

197
00:13:47.710 --> 00:13:49.750
We need to go before
the enemy's gunpowder

198
00:13:49.830 --> 00:13:52.290
stops turning into flowers!

199
00:13:52.490 --> 00:13:54.330
Also... I, uh...

200
00:13:54.720 --> 00:13:57.000
I don't want
your food to get cold!

201
00:13:57.000 --> 00:14:01.160
Because I... I...
I packed you a lunch!

202
00:14:01.180 --> 00:14:02.060
Huh?

203
00:14:02.060 --> 00:14:03.390
Ah! No, I misspoke!

204
00:14:03.790 --> 00:14:05.040
I mean, you misheard me!

205
00:14:11.480 --> 00:14:14.030
Prince!
What's the status?

206
00:14:14.310 --> 00:14:15.480
We're in the clear.

207
00:14:15.820 --> 00:14:17.940
Everything went
off without a hitch.

208
00:14:21.510 --> 00:14:25.260
<b>Rear Admiral Prince Grus</b>
<b>Marine Headquarters</b>

209
00:14:25.260 --> 00:14:27.720
<b>Glorp-Glorp Fruit</b>
<b>Clay Man</b>

210
00:14:25.430 --> 00:14:27.080
Koby's doing fine!

211
00:14:27.720 --> 00:14:30.180
<b>Mud Puppet (Golem)</b>

212
00:14:30.740 --> 00:14:33.290
Wait a sec. This place
doesn't look right.

213
00:14:33.420 --> 00:14:34.190
Where are we?

214
00:14:34.290 --> 00:14:36.290
Huh?

215
00:14:36.290 --> 00:14:40.250
Hey! Everyone, look!
That building just moved!

216
00:14:40.250 --> 00:14:42.130
No! Wait!

217
00:14:45.390 --> 00:14:46.810
It's too late.

218
00:14:46.890 --> 00:14:48.970
They moved the buildings
and trapped us here!

219
00:14:49.050 --> 00:14:49.810
Alright!

220
00:14:49.890 --> 00:14:51.310
Whenever you're ready!

221
00:14:51.390 --> 00:14:52.990
Aim for the dead center!

222
00:14:53.360 --> 00:14:55.570
I just got confirmation
from Prince!

223
00:14:55.870 --> 00:14:59.470
Everyone is in position!
We're ready, Vice Admiral!

224
00:14:59.670 --> 00:15:00.470
Everyone!

225
00:15:01.740 --> 00:15:05.120
Everyone! Hang on tight!

226
00:15:05.610 --> 00:15:07.940
To hell we go!

227
00:15:08.570 --> 00:15:09.970
Ha ha!

228
00:15:15.480 --> 00:15:16.200
Okay!

229
00:15:16.280 --> 00:15:17.110
Hurry!

230
00:15:16.600 --> 00:15:19.560
Alright! If you're
ready, I am, too!

231
00:15:21.060 --> 00:15:22.770
Whoa,
what the hell is that?

232
00:15:22.770 --> 00:15:24.820
I'm not stickin'
around to find out!

233
00:15:24.640 --> 00:15:25.470
A cop!

234
00:15:26.870 --> 00:15:27.670
Huh?

235
00:15:31.090 --> 00:15:31.920
Huh?

236
00:15:32.920 --> 00:15:33.750
Aaaaaaaah!

237
00:15:37.900 --> 00:15:40.460
Aaaaaaaah!

238
00:15:40.540 --> 00:15:42.120
There's an alien
ship in the sky!

239
00:15:42.200 --> 00:15:43.890
It's flying straight for us!

240
00:15:44.220 --> 00:15:46.930
But why?
And how?

241
00:15:47.290 --> 00:15:48.650
Whose
ship is that?

242
00:15:49.400 --> 00:15:51.990
Huh... Looks like it's falling.

243
00:15:51.990 --> 00:15:55.780
We
gotta go! Run away!

244
00:15:58.500 --> 00:16:01.680
No way!
I know that ship!

245
00:16:04.360 --> 00:16:08.020
No. That can't be
right! I thought he retired!

246
00:16:08.020 --> 00:16:11.060
The legendary
hero! He's coming!

247
00:16:16.080 --> 00:16:18.860
It's
Vice Admiral Garp!

248
00:16:19.330 --> 00:16:24.040
Koby! I came to get ya, boy!

249
00:16:24.980 --> 00:16:27.480
Come on! We have
to take cover!

250
00:16:27.480 --> 00:16:31.020
We're trapped! There's
no way outta here!

251
00:16:33.860 --> 00:16:37.650
What?! You wanna
piece of me?!

252
00:16:37.650 --> 00:16:41.240
– Uh! Oh, shit!
– He's coming for us!

253
00:16:59.920 --> 00:17:01.950
I'm not worth any of this!

254
00:17:02.770 --> 00:17:05.650
You would risk starting
a war just to protect me?

255
00:17:06.330 --> 00:17:08.420
Hey, morons!

256
00:17:08.530 --> 00:17:13.570
Who do you think you kidnapped?
Do you know who that kid is?

257
00:17:21.510 --> 00:17:25.380
Koby's not just
the future of the Navy!

258
00:17:25.380 --> 00:17:31.580
That boy...
is my favorite student!

259
00:17:34.380 --> 00:17:39.060
Galaxy Impact!

260
00:17:48.290 --> 00:17:50.630
Impact!

261
00:19:07.720 --> 00:19:11.110
My back! Damn
Garp! He's insane!

262
00:19:11.110 --> 00:19:13.240
Where'd ya go? You're dead!

263
00:19:13.240 --> 00:19:16.130
Hey, pirates! Not so fast!

264
00:19:18.130 --> 00:19:19.930
We've got
plenty more firepower.

265
00:19:27.420 --> 00:19:29.740
Still a few
buildings left.

266
00:19:30.210 --> 00:19:33.030
I must be losin' my touch.

267
00:19:33.030 --> 00:19:34.510
"Losing your touch"?!

268
00:19:34.630 --> 00:19:37.470
Quit rubbin'
it in, you old bastard!

269
00:19:37.490 --> 00:19:38.820
Vice Admiral Garp!

270
00:19:38.850 --> 00:19:43.100
Huh? Hey! There he is!

271
00:19:43.090 --> 00:19:44.790
You all right, Koby?!

272
00:19:47.390 --> 00:19:48.490
I'm so happy!

273
00:19:48.490 --> 00:19:51.440
I thought my buddy
was gonna die!

274
00:19:51.570 --> 00:19:57.280
And once again, Garp overdid it.
Such a naughty boy, isn't he?

275
00:19:57.280 --> 00:20:00.370
I can't believe he said Koby
is the future of the Navy.

276
00:20:00.560 --> 00:20:03.720
As if. I'll put that
kid in his place!

277
00:20:03.720 --> 00:20:06.070
I know you're
too spoiled to know better,

278
00:20:06.070 --> 00:20:09.110
but that's not the sort of thing
you should say out loud.

279
00:20:11.950 --> 00:20:12.910
Captain Koby!

280
00:20:14.710 --> 00:20:15.540
Koby!

281
00:20:18.130 --> 00:20:18.790
Tashigi!

282
00:20:18.870 --> 00:20:21.410
Even people who are from
SWORD are here!

283
00:20:21.260 --> 00:20:25.260
Hm? What have you got
there? A big ball and chain?

284
00:20:25.280 --> 00:20:26.640
We tried, Vice Admiral.

285
00:20:27.830 --> 00:20:30.180
We had no choice
but to take it with us!

286
00:20:30.670 --> 00:20:31.500
It's unfair!

287
00:20:34.500 --> 00:20:35.300
...something?

288
00:20:35.820 --> 00:20:36.620
We can't...

289
00:20:44.110 --> 00:20:44.910
Hibari!

290
00:20:45.540 --> 00:20:46.390
Hibari!

291
00:20:49.740 --> 00:20:51.090
She's frozen solid?

292
00:21:02.460 --> 00:21:03.280
Kuzan.

293
00:21:04.630 --> 00:21:08.430
Why, Kuzan? Why
are you doing this?

294
00:21:08.720 --> 00:21:10.460
Unfreeze Hibari right now!

295
00:21:10.460 --> 00:21:14.800
Woohoo!
Hell yeah, it's Aokiji!

296
00:21:15.180 --> 00:21:16.800
You guys are dead now!

297
00:21:17.500 --> 00:21:18.880
Go, Kuzan!

298
00:21:20.580 --> 00:21:22.520
Don't get
me in trouble, kid.

299
00:21:22.520 --> 00:21:27.620
Can't have you getting away.
How would that look to Teach?

300
00:21:27.620 --> 00:21:29.590
Two years ago,
there was a struggle

301
00:21:29.590 --> 00:21:31.800
to determine who would be
the next Fleet Admiral

302
00:21:31.800 --> 00:21:33.510
at Navy Headquarters.

303
00:21:34.030 --> 00:21:40.170
To that end, Admiral Akainu
and Admiral Aokiji had a duel.

304
00:21:44.060 --> 00:21:46.790
The fight
went on for ten days

305
00:21:46.870 --> 00:21:49.260
before a victor was decided.

306
00:21:49.340 --> 00:21:52.060
Akainu stood triumphant.

307
00:21:52.070 --> 00:21:55.030
Regardless, Aokiji
refused to serve

308
00:21:55.030 --> 00:22:01.540
under Akainu as Fleet Admiral,
and so, he resigned.

309
00:22:05.600 --> 00:22:10.560
<b>Some Island, New World</b>

310
00:22:19.420 --> 00:22:20.590
What the hell?

311
00:22:21.500 --> 00:22:23.750
Blackbeard is here!

312
00:22:23.750 --> 00:22:26.050
Run!
Get outta town while you can!

313
00:22:26.050 --> 00:22:29.340
Hey! What is this?
What happened here?

314
00:22:29.340 --> 00:22:33.260
Stop! Someone tell
me who did this!

315
00:22:36.560 --> 00:22:40.440
Wait,
I know what this is.

316
00:22:40.690 --> 00:22:42.610
I don't even gotta ask.

317
00:22:43.030 --> 00:22:46.440
There's only one guy in the world
who could pull this off!

318
00:22:47.820 --> 00:22:51.740
I thought so! Aokiji!

319
00:23:03.360 --> 00:23:06.780
What's the big idea,
turnin' my crew into ice cubes?

320
00:23:07.400 --> 00:23:08.240
Fix it!

321
00:23:09.510 --> 00:23:11.470
Why don't
you fix your attitude?

322
00:23:14.020 --> 00:23:15.840
Wouldn't do
that if I were you.

323
00:23:16.470 --> 00:23:19.440
Your friends'll shatter and die.

324
00:23:20.930 --> 00:23:25.310
C'mon, now. You think
I started this fight?

325
00:23:25.370 --> 00:23:28.740
You know what kinad
company you keep.

326
00:23:29.220 --> 00:23:32.230
Also, I'm sure you heard
the news about me.

327
00:23:32.650 --> 00:23:38.120
I'm in a state of mourning.
You shouldn't test me.

328
00:23:38.630 --> 00:23:41.780
So let's cool it
with the demands, shall we?

329
00:23:50.160 --> 00:23:57.020
Ze-ze-ze-ze-ze-

330
00:24:06.150 --> 00:24:07.750
Who's ready for more?

331
00:24:13.080 --> 00:24:15.420
You're not so bad
yourself, shitbag!

332
00:24:18.210 --> 00:24:21.400
Okay, before the battle,
what does Akainu say?

333
00:24:24.700 --> 00:24:27.910
"We climbed the ranks together,
now we fight to the death.

334
00:24:28.210 --> 00:24:31.040
I'm starting to feel a hot
lump in my throat."

335
00:24:31.370 --> 00:24:35.170
That's what he said.
And you know what I told him?

336
00:24:35.170 --> 00:24:37.920
"No shit, asshole,
you're made of magma!"

337
00:24:40.470 --> 00:24:42.450
Look what that bastard did!

338
00:24:43.150 --> 00:24:47.510
Took off my whole damn leg!

339
00:24:47.930 --> 00:24:49.970
So that's what happens
when two admirals

340
00:24:49.970 --> 00:24:51.430
decide to throw down, huh?

341
00:24:51.430 --> 00:24:56.090
So'd you pay him back, or what?
Rip off one of his arms, maybe?

342
00:24:56.090 --> 00:24:57.650
Nah.

343
00:24:59.710 --> 00:25:02.620
But he's got some scars
to remember me by.

344
00:25:03.300 --> 00:25:07.180
That reminds
me, Commodore.

345
00:25:07.490 --> 00:25:09.860
He might know the Man
with the Burn Scar.

346
00:25:09.990 --> 00:25:12.240
The what? Who
the hell's that?

347
00:25:12.240 --> 00:25:15.160
For real? So you
haven't heard?

348
00:25:14.410 --> 00:25:19.090
We gotta find the four
Road Poneglyphs.

349
00:25:15.160 --> 00:25:17.580
The deal is, if we wanna
make it to Laugh Tale,

350
00:25:19.090 --> 00:25:22.350
Ys know 'em when you see 'em,
'cause they're bright red.

351
00:25:22.820 --> 00:25:25.330
Kaido and Big Mom
have one each.

352
00:25:26.270 --> 00:25:30.640
But what about the other two?
They're still a mystery!

353
00:25:30.710 --> 00:25:33.290
We're just hoping fate
will guide us to them.

354
00:25:33.370 --> 00:25:34.460
That's right.

355
00:25:34.540 --> 00:25:36.900
Well, we do have
one tiny lead.

356
00:25:36.900 --> 00:25:40.990
We heard some man with a burn
scar has one of them.

357
00:25:42.370 --> 00:25:43.500
You mean me?

358
00:25:43.500 --> 00:25:45.850
No, not you! You just
got that the other day!

359
00:25:48.020 --> 00:25:53.360
Quite
the mystery, no?

360
00:25:58.410 --> 00:26:00.920
Rumor has it that
the Man with the Burn Scar

361
00:26:00.920 --> 00:26:03.340
sails on a pitch-black ship.

362
00:26:10.300 --> 00:26:12.300
But if
anyone approaches it,

363
00:26:12.300 --> 00:26:14.310
their ship will be
whisked away,

364
00:26:14.310 --> 00:26:18.140
swallowed up by
a giant whirlpool.

365
00:26:20.930 --> 00:26:23.640
I'd assume the fellow
has a devil fruit power.

366
00:26:24.310 --> 00:26:25.370
Just a hunch,

367
00:26:25.450 --> 00:26:27.700
but I bet the guy is
with the Government.

368
00:26:28.390 --> 00:26:29.740
They've got their hands
in everything,

369
00:26:29.740 --> 00:26:32.230
and plenty of dark secrets.

370
00:26:32.240 --> 00:26:34.880
They know everyone
needs those stones.

371
00:26:34.900 --> 00:26:37.990
If they had one, all they'd
have to do is hold on to it...

372
00:26:37.990 --> 00:26:39.260
...and we'd be sunk.

373
00:26:39.580 --> 00:26:43.850
No pirate could find their way
to Laugh Tale or the One Piece.

374
00:26:44.720 --> 00:26:48.300
The Poneglyphs, huh?
Brings back memories.

375
00:26:48.300 --> 00:26:49.570
Hate to break it to ya,

376
00:26:49.570 --> 00:26:52.240
but I never saw a giant
red stone in Ohara.

377
00:26:52.970 --> 00:26:54.040
I'd remember.

378
00:26:55.540 --> 00:26:58.380
I haven't forgotten
a thing about that day.

379
00:26:58.460 --> 00:27:01.890
The day I watched my best friend
rebel against the Government.

380
00:27:01.890 --> 00:27:04.460
And the day that I
saw those sad eyes.

381
00:27:04.460 --> 00:27:08.890
When I held that poor,
lonely girl's fate in my hands.

382
00:27:08.890 --> 00:27:13.290
Huh? That story sounds
boring as all hell!

383
00:27:16.400 --> 00:27:19.040
Commodore,
what should we do?

384
00:27:19.710 --> 00:27:21.900
A power like his could be
quite useful.

385
00:27:21.980 --> 00:27:24.330
I say we take it while
his guard's down.

386
00:27:28.080 --> 00:27:29.280
Huh?

387
00:27:29.620 --> 00:27:32.540
I heard that,
you conniving bastards!

388
00:27:34.620 --> 00:27:35.660
C'mon, then!

389
00:27:35.960 --> 00:27:39.040
You wanna know what it
feels like to freeze to death?

390
00:27:42.420 --> 00:27:43.990
Take it easy, buddy!

391
00:27:44.470 --> 00:27:47.190
So
the rumors are true.

392
00:27:47.200 --> 00:27:48.200
You're hunting people

393
00:27:48.200 --> 00:27:51.620
with strong devil fruit
powers, aren't you?

394
00:27:51.620 --> 00:27:55.420
Then try to take
mine! I dare you!

395
00:27:58.000 --> 00:27:58.800
Yeah!

396
00:27:59.370 --> 00:28:02.460
Whoa, whoa! Listen to me!

397
00:28:02.460 --> 00:28:05.840
My crew members were
getting carried away, that's all!

398
00:28:06.380 --> 00:28:08.920
Let me apologize
on their behalf.

399
00:28:08.920 --> 00:28:11.470
I don't wanna
steal your power.

400
00:28:11.470 --> 00:28:13.470
I want you to join my crew!

401
00:28:15.510 --> 00:28:17.720
Are you nuts? An ex-Marine?

402
00:28:17.720 --> 00:28:20.770
Why not? You're out
of a job now, right?

403
00:28:20.770 --> 00:28:24.480
You got any place to go?
Anything you're planning to do?

404
00:28:24.540 --> 00:28:27.210
Not gonna be defending
justice anymore.

405
00:28:27.250 --> 00:28:30.260
Ha! Guess I've sunk
pretty low, huh?

406
00:28:30.260 --> 00:28:31.990
A good-for-nothing
pirate's worried about

407
00:28:31.990 --> 00:28:33.760
the state of my employment.

408
00:28:34.190 --> 00:28:37.120
Men like us will find
trouble anywhere we go.

409
00:28:37.860 --> 00:28:40.790
Can't run, so you might
as well face it head-on.

410
00:28:41.230 --> 00:28:42.890
What flag will you fly?

411
00:28:42.930 --> 00:28:44.060
When you put
your life on the line,

412
00:28:44.060 --> 00:28:45.830
what will you be fighting for?

413
00:28:46.140 --> 00:28:46.970
Tell me!

414
00:28:49.130 --> 00:28:52.020
I've got my own brand
of justice, my own code!

415
00:28:52.100 --> 00:28:55.010
This won't be nothing like
the Navy, I promise you!

416
00:28:55.090 --> 00:28:56.070
Yeah, I'm sure!

417
00:28:56.180 --> 00:28:58.220
But I'll still get stabbed
straight in the back!

418
00:28:58.220 --> 00:29:01.310
You think sharin' a couple
of drinks means I can trust you?

419
00:29:01.380 --> 00:29:02.560
Of course not!

420
00:29:02.640 --> 00:29:05.420
I don't think you understand
how pirates work!

421
00:29:05.500 --> 00:29:07.290
We're not here
to make friends!

422
00:29:07.370 --> 00:29:09.610
We're a crew, but we're
not buddy-buddy!

423
00:29:14.750 --> 00:29:16.770
We all have a common goal!

424
00:29:18.950 --> 00:29:23.300
All pirates need is
an alignment of interests!

425
00:29:26.060 --> 00:29:30.610
You're free now,
Kuzan. Your choice.

426
00:29:31.240 --> 00:29:33.000
What do you really want?

427
00:29:47.830 --> 00:29:52.080
Stop this, Kuzan!
Thaw Hibari out right now!

428
00:29:52.120 --> 00:29:54.080
Let Koby escape from here!

429
00:29:54.160 --> 00:29:56.720
Come back to the Navy!

430
00:29:59.240 --> 00:30:02.200
Y'never change, huh?
Can't stop to think.

431
00:30:02.610 --> 00:30:04.160
You just run your mouth.

432
00:30:08.410 --> 00:30:11.260
But I'm afraid I can't
help you today, Garp!

433
00:30:11.340 --> 00:30:12.460
I'm sorry!

434
00:30:13.090 --> 00:30:17.330
You've always been
straightforward. I admire that.

435
00:30:17.330 --> 00:30:18.390
You inspired me.

436
00:30:18.390 --> 00:30:21.650
So I'm livin' the way
I want to now!

437
00:30:19.710 --> 00:30:22.720
<b>Kuzan
Captain of the Tenth Ship
Blackbeard Pirates</b>

438
00:30:27.620 --> 00:30:28.900
You damn fool.

439
00:30:46.120 --> 00:30:47.420
Ice Ball!

440
00:30:55.260 --> 00:30:56.610
Vice Admiral Garp!

441
00:30:58.610 --> 00:30:59.790
Vice Admiral!

442
00:31:04.300 --> 00:31:07.120
Your old student
and your new student...

443
00:31:07.770 --> 00:31:11.650
Would you do anything to save
Koby, even if it kills me?

444
00:31:11.710 --> 00:31:16.970
Heh. What are you doing,
bringing up the past?

445
00:31:17.100 --> 00:31:19.840
I taught you to live
in the moment, didn't I?

446
00:31:25.680 --> 00:31:27.500
How the hell did
he break free?!

447
00:31:47.580 --> 00:31:48.990
Here's another lesson!

448
00:32:12.510 --> 00:32:14.360
Men who waver...

449
00:32:16.510 --> 00:32:17.670
...are weak!

450
00:32:19.360 --> 00:32:23.320
Come on! Blue Hole!

451
00:32:32.200 --> 00:32:33.030
Meanwhile,

452
00:32:51.950 --> 00:32:57.120
<b>Winner Island
New World</b>

453
00:32:53.120 --> 00:32:55.000
On the coast
of Winter Island...

454
00:33:13.550 --> 00:33:14.350
Zee!

455
00:33:17.280 --> 00:33:18.080
Zee!

456
00:33:32.570 --> 00:33:34.570
Now that your ship
is out of the picture,

457
00:33:34.570 --> 00:33:38.030
you haven't just lost your right
to call yourself a pirate,

458
00:33:38.030 --> 00:33:41.240
you've lost your only escape.

459
00:33:41.240 --> 00:33:44.200
You stole 100 hearts
that day at Rocky Port.

460
00:33:44.200 --> 00:33:47.420
You had to expect some
kinda payback from me!

461
00:33:47.420 --> 00:33:49.380
Those poor pirates
back at my base,

462
00:33:49.380 --> 00:33:52.380
living every damn day in fear!

463
00:33:52.380 --> 00:33:55.300
So I think I'll bring them
back your heart as a gift!

464
00:33:55.300 --> 00:33:58.850
Bet that'll have the sad
bastards jumpin' for joy!

465
00:33:58.970 --> 00:33:59.270
Zee!

466
00:33:59.350 --> 00:34:01.310
Ha ha ha ha ha ha ha ha ha!

467
00:34:05.670 --> 00:34:07.800
Oh, wow, you
made this for me?

468
00:34:07.880 --> 00:34:09.460
But I haven't been
able to test it,

469
00:34:09.460 --> 00:34:12.090
so I can't guarantee it'll work.

470
00:34:17.680 --> 00:34:19.080
Let me think.

471
00:34:19.170 --> 00:34:20.380
We could sell your Fruit,

472
00:34:20.380 --> 00:34:23.380
but I think I could put
it to better use.

473
00:34:23.380 --> 00:34:27.660
They say it can grant
someone eternal life, right?

474
00:34:32.870 --> 00:34:36.500
You... stay away!

475
00:34:38.660 --> 00:34:39.440
Huh?

476
00:34:39.520 --> 00:34:40.960
That's my captain!

477
00:34:49.130 --> 00:34:50.970
Bepo.

478
00:34:50.160 --> 00:34:51.860
That bear...

479
00:34:56.140 --> 00:35:01.310
It can't be! Sulong? But how?
The moon isn't even out!

480
00:35:52.610 --> 00:35:55.020
Damn it! They're
headed to the sea!

481
00:35:55.550 --> 00:35:56.720
Get them, now!

482
00:36:02.300 --> 00:36:06.770
Take me back, Bepo.

483
00:36:11.600 --> 00:36:15.680
They're my friends.
I can't leave them.

484
00:36:15.820 --> 00:36:19.530
I'm sorry, Captain!
We can't risk it!

485
00:36:19.680 --> 00:36:25.200
But your crew was forged
in the cold waters of the north!

486
00:36:26.470 --> 00:36:27.770
Have faith in them!

487
00:36:27.770 --> 00:36:31.490
Through every fight,
they've held strong!

488
00:36:31.890 --> 00:36:33.560
They won't die here!

489
00:36:40.010 --> 00:36:42.410
We've overcome
so much together!

490
00:36:44.250 --> 00:36:49.470
We have
to survive! All of us!

491
00:36:58.970 --> 00:37:03.890
Don't die,
Captain! We need you!

492
00:37:07.980 --> 00:37:11.570
The battle at Winner
Island, in the New World,

493
00:37:11.570 --> 00:37:13.990
came to an end.

494
00:37:19.930 --> 00:37:22.800
Blackbeard
destroyed the Polar Tang,

495
00:37:22.800 --> 00:37:25.680
the submarine
of the Heart Pirates,

496
00:37:26.950 --> 00:37:29.070
and it sank into the sea.

497
00:37:31.610 --> 00:37:38.050
The Heart Pirates, led by
Trafalgar Law, were defeated.
